te": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 375784, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017jXFPwMXxDj6hwJi5DxmrV", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 379648, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The problem:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` was rounding halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding per FIN-212. Banker's rounding sends halves to the nearest even cent, so 2.665 \u2192 2.66 and 2.675 \u2192 2.68, which is what the test expects.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed it to banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI haven't merged it. Policy says merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JQY4vjbJmkeNAPUyhx5Gma", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016jU23HNtginobY827YF1cg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01U169oJzcbMcf8eraWf6fPZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014VwmkszpHx5av8cy7KjY8o", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": n